\section{Proposed Solution %
\BvrHint{\ldots Software Proposition}}
\subsection{Overview}
Medkart.ai implements a \textbf{web-based} prescription-to-comparison pipeline across 5 Indian e-pharmacy platforms (1mg, PharmEasy, Netmeds, Truemeds, Apollo 24\slash{}7), consisting of a React web application and backend microservices covering OCR, structuring, normalization, fetching, AI enrichment, ranking, and realtime delivery:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=0.7cm]
    \item \textbf{Web application:} prescription upload with OCR, direct search, real-time comparison, anomaly explanations, interaction warnings, watchlist alerts.
    \item \textbf{OCR \& structuring pipeline:} extracts drug name\slash{}dosage\slash{}frequency; an LLM converts raw OCR text to structured fields.
    \item \textbf{Normalization layer:} fuzzy-matches names to a canonical catalog; resolves brand to salt; logs match confidence.
    \item \textbf{Hybrid fetch layer:} routes each platform to a static scraper or headless browser; applies anti-bot measures; checks Redis before scraping.
    \item \textbf{AI-enrichment engine:} Isolation Forest anomaly detection vs.\ NPPA with SHAP explanations; generic-substitute ranking; LLM-based interaction checking with safety guardrails.
    \item \textbf{Ranking \& realtime layer:} weighted scoring by price\slash{}discount\slash{}delivery\slash{}stock; progressive WebSocket\slash{}SSE streaming.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Core workflow}
\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=0.7cm]
    \item Patient uploads a prescription image or searches directly.
    \item OCR extracts text; the structuring service parses it into drug\slash{}dosage\slash{}frequency fields.
    \item Normalization maps names to canonical salts, logging match confidence.
    \item The fetch service retrieves live prices from all 5 platforms (cache-first, with scrape fallback).
    \item AI-enrichment flags anomalous prices (SHAP-explained) and checks drug interactions.
    \item Ranking orders results; the realtime service streams them progressively to the patient.
    \item Patient may watchlist a medicine for target-price alerts.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Operational constraints for a campus-pilot setting}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=0.7cm]
    \item Establish a rule-based\slash{}heuristic baseline (fixed-threshold NPPA deviation, keyword-match interaction check) before any ML component, so evaluation always has a non-ML floor to beat.
    \item Use only publicly published NPPA ceiling-price data and document data provenance to avoid licensing risk.
    \item Keep OCR human-correctable and provide a direct-search fallback so the system remains usable even when scanning fails.
    \item Design for deployability using Docker Compose for local development and a single managed-cloud target (AWS) for the pilot.
\end{itemize}

\section{Solution Approach %
\BvrHint{\ldots Engineering focus}}
This is an engineering course project, so we focus on a working pipeline with a measurable baseline rather than novel algorithm research.

\subsection{Price-anomaly detection approach %
\BvrHint{\ldots baseline before ML}}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=0.7cm]
    \item Build a labelled dataset (normal, mildly overpriced, severely overpriced vs.\ NPPA ceiling).
    \item Use a rule-based fixed-threshold baseline for comparison.
    \item Develop the Isolation Forest detector with SHAP explainability and compare against the baseline on held-out data.
\end{itemize}

