\section{Risks and mitigations}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=0.7cm]
    \item \textbf{Scraper fragility:} hybrid connector design, scraper-regression tests, cached fallback (FR-12\slash{}13, NFR-5).
    \item \textbf{Data licensing:} use only publicly published NPPA data; document provenance.
    \item \textbf{OCR accuracy:} human-in-the-loop correction; direct-search fallback (FR-6).
    \item \textbf{LLM hallucination:} mandatory safety-guardrail layer before output reaches user (FR-21, NFR-9).
    \item \textbf{Evaluation measurement ambiguity:} finalize the labelled-dataset protocol before development begins.
    \item \textbf{Pilot operational issues:} early staging use; repeatable CI\slash{}CD; cross-device OCR\slash{}scraping tests.
\end{itemize}

\section{Summary}
This project proposes Medkart.ai, a deployable web platform that verifies medicine price fairness against government-regulated ceilings and checks drug-interaction safety within the same pipeline used for price comparison across 5 major Indian e-pharmacy platforms. It meets the course criteria by emphasizing time-to-value through rapid iterations, implementing CI\slash{}CD to support frequent safe releases, and using measurable evaluation criteria (especially the anomaly-detector F1 score against a rule-based baseline). It remains focused on engineering pipeline correctness and scalability readiness, validated through a campus pilot of approximately 40--60 students and staff, with full traceability to the functional and non-functional requirements above.

